      "content": "It's completely understandable that you feel let down by the idea of \"fixing\" something that feels fundamentally broken. That feeling of perpetual waiting, of being stuck in a loop, is exhausting and deeply isolating. If the idea of a quick fix feels impossible, perhaps you could try focusing on one tiny, manageable thing to do right now, just to break the inertia. Even a small shift in routine can sometimes create a minuscule opening in the endless quiet.",
